      "description": "Core's own executable surface, with every test beside its subject: the review-comment Tool and its move helper, the glossary extractors and builder (`build-glossary.ts`, its `:refterm` codemod `codemod-refterm.ts`), the sample-import pair, the materialisation trio (`check-materialized-fixity`, `backfill-materialized-fixity`, `cache-index`), `check-voices.ts` (every voice rule's citation resolved through `schemas/library-ref.ts` into a folio's `library/`), `build-document-site.ts` (which reads `schemas/changeset.ts`), and the document, bibliography, public-comment and tabular tools. Pipeline scripts are addressed by id, and `resolvePipelineScript` searches the folio, then the platform, then here. Two scripts are invocation surfaces, named by path and so not to be moved without updating their callers: `build-document-site.ts`, which a DOCUMENT folio's generated staging workflow names (`init-folio.ts` writes `folio-assistant-core/scripts/build-document-site.ts` and `init-folio.test.ts` pins it), and `review-comments.ts`, invoked by path from `folio-staging.yml`.",
